IMPORT prelude

-- Internal Security Act 1960 (Singapore) -- the offences an ordinary person can commit under Part 2 (uniforms, quasi-military
-- associations, drilling, banned and subversive publications, false reports) and their penalties (ss 4-7, 20-27, 45); the firearm
-- offence in a security area (s 58); the time limits and safeguards of preventive detention (ss 8, 8B, 11, 12, 13, 13A); and the
-- procedural consequences in Part 4 (ss 73, 80, 81).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/ISA1960.txt, with amendments
-- to Act 3 of 2021 (in force 1 July 2025) shown. NOTE: the arrangement of sections in the deposit is out of step with the body in
-- Part 2 Chapter 6; this module follows the BODY's numbering (s 44 attempts, s 45 general penalty, s 46 arrest, s 47 bonds).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 11 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository. SCOPED to what a person can be charged with
-- and what a detainee is owed in time. Not encoded: the Minister's and President's discretions themselves (whether to detain or to
-- ban a publication), search and seizure (ss 28, 29, 34-36), entertainments and exhibitions (ss 30-39), schools and education
-- (ss 40-43), security-area powers other than s 58 (ss 48-57, 59-72), suspected-person detention (s 74), lethal force (s 75),
-- evidence (ss 76, 77), and the Schedules.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules conventions as shown in earlier rows. No pipeline,
-- no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Internal Security Act 1960 -- offences and detention`

§§ `Offences and their maximum penalties`

DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `wearing a prohibited political uniform`
    `being a member of a quasi-military association`
    `organising or managing a quasi-military association`
    `attending unauthorised drilling`
    `training others in drilling or managing a drilling association`
    `breaching an emblem or flag order`
    `printing or selling a banned publication`
    `possessing a banned publication, first offence`
    `possessing a banned publication, subsequent offence`
    `importing a banned publication, first offence`
    `importing a banned publication, subsequent offence`
    `posting an inciting placard`
    `spreading false reports likely to cause public alarm`
    `possessing a subversive document`
    `carrying a firearm in a security area`

-- s 4: wearing a uniform prohibited under s 3 -- "a fine not exceeding $2,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding one year".
-- s 5(1): a "member or adherent" of an association organised, trained or equipped to usurp the police or the Armed Forces, or to
-- use or display physical force in promoting "any political or other object" -- $2,000 or one year; a person who "promotes ... or
-- who takes part in the control or management of" it -- $10,000 or 5 years.
-- s 6(1): attending a meeting for drilling in arms or military exercises -- $2,000 or one year. s 6(2): training or drilling any
-- other person, or managing an association whose members are drilled -- $10,000 or 5 years.
-- s 7(2): contravening an order on flags, badges, emblems or uniforms is an offence, with no penalty stated in s 7.
-- s 22: printing, publishing, selling, issuing, circulating or reproducing a document banned under s 20 -- $2,000 or 3 years.
-- s 23(1): possessing a banned document without lawful excuse -- first offence $1,000 or one year; "in respect of a subsequent
-- offence to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 2 years". s 24: importing -- first offence $1,000 or 2 years; subsequent
-- offence imprisonment up to 3 years.
-- ss 25, 26: posting inciting placards and spreading "false reports ... likely to cause public alarm" are offences, with no penalty
-- in the section.
-- s 45: contravention "for which no special penalty is provided" -- "a fine not exceeding $1,000 or to imprisonment for a term not
-- exceeding one year or to both". Applied here to ss 7, 25 and 26.
-- s 27(1): possessing a subversive document without lawful excuse -- $10,000 or 5 years.
-- s 58(1): in a security area, carrying a firearm, ammunition or explosive without lawful authority or excuse -- "liable on
-- conviction to be punished with death".
--
-- For a subsequent offence under ss 23 and 24 the text states imprisonment only. Encoding that as "no fine" (0 below) is an
-- INFERENCE from the wording, not something the text says in terms.
GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the maximum fine` IS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `wearing a prohibited political uniform` THEN 2000
    WHEN `being a member of a quasi-military association` THEN 2000
    WHEN `organising or managing a quasi-military association` THEN 10000
    WHEN `attending unauthorised drilling` THEN 2000
    WHEN `training others in drilling or managing a drilling association` THEN 10000
    WHEN `breaching an emblem or flag order` THEN 1000
    WHEN `printing or selling a banned publication` THEN 2000
    WHEN `possessing a banned publication, first offence` THEN 1000
    WHEN `possessing a banned publication, subsequent offence` THEN 0
    WHEN `importing a banned publication, first offence` THEN 1000
    WHEN `importing a banned publication, subsequent offence` THEN 0
    WHEN `posting an inciting placard` THEN 1000
    WHEN `spreading false reports likely to cause public alarm` THEN 1000
    WHEN `possessing a subversive document` THEN 10000
    WHEN `carrying a firearm in a security area` THEN 0

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the maximum imprisonment in years` IS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `wearing a prohibited political uniform` THEN 1
    WHEN `being a member of a quasi-military association` THEN 1
    WHEN `organising or managing a quasi-military association` THEN 5
    WHEN `attending unauthorised drilling` THEN 1
    WHEN `training others in drilling or managing a drilling association` THEN 5
    WHEN `breaching an emblem or flag order` THEN 1
    WHEN `printing or selling a banned publication` THEN 3
    WHEN `possessing a banned publication, first offence` THEN 1
    WHEN `possessing a banned publication, subsequent offence` THEN 2
    WHEN `importing a banned publication, first offence` THEN 2
    WHEN `importing a banned publication, subsequent offence` THEN 3
    WHEN `posting an inciting placard` THEN 1
    WHEN `spreading false reports likely to cause public alarm` THEN 1
    WHEN `possessing a subversive document` THEN 5
    WHEN `carrying a firearm in a security area` THEN 0

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the offence is punishable with death` IF
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `carrying a firearm in a security area` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `73, 80, 81 and 5(2) -- bail, court and consent`

-- s 73(1): every offence under the Act is seizable. (2): "Every offence under this Act punishable with imprisonment for a term
-- exceeding 3 years shall be non-bailable". s 58(4): "A person charged with an offence under this section shall not be granted
-- bail."
GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the offence is non-bailable` IF
        `the maximum imprisonment in years` `the offence` > 3
    OR  `the offence is punishable with death` `the offence`

-- s 81: a prosecution for an offence "punishable with imprisonment for a term of 7 years or more" needs the Public Prosecutor's
-- consent. s 5(2): "No prosecution for any offence under this section shall be instituted except with the consent of the Public
-- Prosecutor." No offence in this module carries 7 years or more of imprisonment, so in scope only s 5 needs consent.
GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Public Prosecutor must consent to prosecution` IF
        `the maximum imprisonment in years` `the offence` >= 7
    OR  CONSIDER `the offence`
        WHEN `being a member of a quasi-military association` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `organising or managing a quasi-military association` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 80: a District Court may try any offence "other than an offence punishable with death", and pass a sentence "not exceeding
-- 5 years' imprisonment or a fine of $5,000 or both".
GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a District Court may try the offence` IF
    NOT `the offence is punishable with death` `the offence`

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a District Court may impose the full maximum` IF
        `a District Court may try the offence` `the offence`
    AND `the maximum imprisonment in years` `the offence` <= 5
    AND `the maximum fine` `the offence` <= 5000

§§ `5 and 6 -- defences and exemptions`

-- s 5(1) proviso: on a charge "of taking part in the control or management of such an association" it is a defence "to prove
-- that he neither consented to nor connived at the organisation, training or equipment". The proviso is limited to that charge.
GIVEN `charged with control or management` IS A BOOLEAN, `proved no consent or connivance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the s 5 management defence succeeds` IF
    `charged with control or management` AND `proved no consent or connivance`

-- s 5(7): nothing prohibits "the employment of a reasonable number of persons as stewards at any public meeting held upon
-- private premises with the permission of the owner of those premises", nor their badges.
GIVEN `a reasonable number` IS A BOOLEAN, `a public meeting on private premises` IS A BOOLEAN, `the owner permitted it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the stewards are saved by s 5(7)` IF
    `a reasonable number` AND `a public meeting on private premises` AND `the owner permitted it`

DECLARE Force IS ONE OF
    `the Singapore Armed Forces`
    `the police`
    `a volunteer or local force under written law`
    `a visiting force`
    `an association exempted by the Minister`
    `no force`

-- s 6(1), (2): "Any person other than a member of the Singapore Armed Forces or the police or of a volunteer force or local force
-- constituted under any written law ..., or of any other force which is a visiting force ... or of any organisation or
-- association specially exempted by the Minister".
GIVEN `the force` IS A Force
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `outside the drilling offences` IF
    CONSIDER `the force`
    WHEN `no force` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 6(1): attending a drilling meeting, whether to be trained "or" to train others -- $2,000 / one year. s 6(2): "trains or
-- drills any other person", or "takes part in the control or management" of a drilling association -- $10,000 / 5 years. A
-- person present to train others falls under both s 6(1)(b) and s 6(2)(a); the higher limit is taken here, which is an
-- INFERENCE (the text does not say which charge is laid).
GIVEN `the force` IS A Force, `attended a drilling meeting` IS A BOOLEAN, `trained others` IS A BOOLEAN, `managed a drilling association` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Offence
DECIDE `the drilling charge` IS
    IF `trained others` OR `managed a drilling association`
    THEN `training others in drilling or managing a drilling association`
    ELSE `attending unauthorised drilling`

GIVEN `the force` IS A Force, `attended a drilling meeting` IS A BOOLEAN, `trained others` IS A BOOLEAN, `managed a drilling association` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a drilling offence is committed` IF
        (NOT `outside the drilling offences` `the force`)
    AND (`attended a drilling meeting` OR `trained others` OR `managed a drilling association`)

§§ `20-24, 27 -- banned and subversive documents`

-- s 21: the proprietor or agent "may, within one month of the date of publication of the order in the Gazette, make an objection
-- against the order to the President, whose decision shall be final".
GIVEN `months since the Gazette order` IS A NUMBER, `is the proprietor or agent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an objection may be made` IF
    `is the proprietor or agent` AND `months since the Gazette order` <= 1

-- s 22 proviso: no conviction if he proves the document was printed etc. "without his authority, consent and knowledge, and
-- without any want of due care or caution on his part, and that he did not know and had no reason to suspect the nature".
-- All three limbs are needed.
GIVEN `without authority consent and knowledge` IS A BOOLEAN, `no want of due care` IS A BOOLEAN, `no reason to suspect` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the s 22 defence succeeds` IF
    `without authority consent and knowledge` AND `no want of due care` AND `no reason to suspect`

-- s 27(4) proviso: no conviction if he proves "(a) that he was not aware of the contents ...; and (b) ... at no time did he have
-- reasonable cause to believe or suspect that such document was a subversive document". Both on him; the document is presumed
-- subversive and he is deemed to know its contents.
GIVEN `proved unaware of the contents` IS A BOOLEAN, `proved no reasonable cause to suspect` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the s 27 defence succeeds` IF
    `proved unaware of the contents` AND `proved no reasonable cause to suspect`

-- s 27(2): any person who receives a subversive document "shall deliver the same without delay to a police officer"; failing to,
-- or communicating or publishing its contents "unless authorised to do so by a police officer not below the rank of
-- superintendent", is an offence -- $10,000 or 5 years.
GIVEN `received a subversive document` IS A BOOLEAN, `delivered it to police without delay` IS A BOOLEAN, `communicated its contents` IS A BOOLEAN, `authorised by a superintendent or above` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the s 27(2) duty is breached` IF
        `received a subversive document`
    AND (    (NOT `delivered it to police without delay`)
         OR  (`communicated its contents` AND (NOT `authorised by a superintendent or above`)))

§§ `58 -- firearms in a security area`

-- s 58(2): lawful authority only if (a) police, security forces or Prisons staff acting in the performance of duty; (b) licensed
-- or authorised under written law; or (c) exempted. Proviso: no one has lawful authority, or is exempt, if he has it "for the
-- purpose of using the same in a manner prejudicial to public security or the maintenance of public order".
-- s 58(1): the offence needs absence of lawful authority AND absence of lawful excuse, "the onus of proving which shall be on such
-- person". s 58(3): lawful excuse only if he proves lawful acquisition for a lawful purpose and no prejudicial conduct.
GIVEN `on duty as police, security forces or prisons staff` IS A BOOLEAN, `licensed` IS A BOOLEAN, `exempted` IS A BOOLEAN, `held for a prejudicial purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `has lawful authority under s 58` IF
        (`on duty as police, security forces or prisons staff` OR `licensed` OR `exempted`)
    AND (NOT `held for a prejudicial purpose`)

GIVEN `in a security area` IS A BOOLEAN, `lawful authority` IS A BOOLEAN, `proved lawful acquisition and purpose` IS A BOOLEAN, `acted prejudicially` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the s 58 offence is committed` IF
        `in a security area`
    AND (NOT `lawful authority`)
    AND (    (NOT `proved lawful acquisition and purpose`)
         OR  `acted prejudicially`)

§§ `8, 8B, 11, 12, 13, 13A -- preventive detention`

-- s 8(1): a detention order "for any period not exceeding 2 years"; a restriction order "for such period, not exceeding 2 years".
-- s 8(2): the President "may direct that the period ... be extended for a further period or periods not exceeding 2 years at a
-- time". No limit on the number of extensions appears in the text.
GIVEN `years` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the period of an order or extension is lawful` IF
    `years` > 0 AND `years` <= 2

-- s 11(2): within 14 days of service of the order the detainee must be informed of the right to make representations and
-- furnished with a statement of grounds, allegations of fact and other particulars.
GIVEN `days since service` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the s 11(2) statement is in time` IF
    `days since service` <= 14

-- s 12(1): where representations are made, the advisory board "shall, within 3 months of the date on which such person was
-- detained, consider such representations and make recommendations thereon to the President".
GIVEN `months since detention` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the advisory board report is in time` IF
    `months since detention` <= 3

DECLARE Subject IS ONE OF
    `a detainee whose representations were considered`
    `a detainee who made no representations`
    `a person under a restriction order`
    `a detainee released under a suspension direction`

-- s 13(1): reviews "at intervals of not more than 12 months"; the first within (a) 12 months from consideration of representations,
-- or 15 months from detention where none were made; (b) 12 months from service for a person not detained; (c) 12 months from
-- release under s 10.
GIVEN `the subject` IS A Subject
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `months allowed until first review` IS
    CONSIDER `the subject`
    WHEN `a detainee who made no representations` THEN 15
    OTHERWISE 12

-- s 13A: where an advisory board recommends release under s 12 or 13, "the person shall not be detained or further detained
-- without the President's concurrence under Article 151(4) of the Constitution".
GIVEN `the board recommended release` IS A BOOLEAN, `the President concurs in detention` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `further detention is permitted` IF
    (NOT `the board recommended release`) OR `the President concurs in detention`

-- s 8B(2): "There shall be no judicial review in any court of any act done or decision made by the President or the Minister under
-- the provisions of this Act save in regard to any question relating to compliance with any procedural requirement".
GIVEN `the question is procedural compliance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a court may review the decision` IF
    `the question is procedural compliance`
